class Solution {
public:

    /*
    PROBLEM: MAXIMUM NUMBER OF VOWELS IN A SUBSTRING OF SIZE K
    ==========================================================

    APPROACH: FIXED SIZE SLIDING WINDOW

    PROBLEM UNDERSTANDING:
    We are given a string str and an integer k.

    We need to find the maximum number of vowels present in
    any contiguous substring of length k.

    Vowels are: a, e, i, o, u.

    Example:
    str = "abciiidef"
    k = 3

    Substrings of size 3:
    "abc" -> 1 vowel
    "bci" -> 1 vowel
    "cii" -> 2 vowels
    "iii" -> 3 vowels
    "ide" -> 2 vowels
    "def" -> 1 vowel

    Answer = 3


    MAIN IDEA:
    ==========
    We use a fixed-size sliding window of size k.

    Instead of counting vowels again in every substring,
    we maintain a variable count.

    - When a vowel enters the window, increase count.
    - When a vowel leaves the window, decrease count.
    - Update ans whenever the window size becomes k.


    ALGORITHM:
    ==========

    STEP 1:
    Initialize two pointers i and j at index 0.

    STEP 2:
    Traverse the string using pointer j.

    STEP 3:
    Check whether the current character str[j] is a vowel.
    If yes, increase count.

    STEP 4:
    When the window size becomes k:
    - Update ans with the maximum value of ans and count.
    - Remove the leftmost character from the window.
    - If that character is a vowel, decrease count.
    - Move i forward.

    STEP 5:
    Move j forward and continue.

    STEP 6:
    Return ans.


    TIME COMPLEXITY:
    =================
    O(n)

    We traverse the string only once.
    Each character is processed a constant number of times.


    AUXILIARY SPACE:
    ===============
    O(1)

    We use only a few variables.
    */


    int maxVowels(string str, int k) {

        int n = str.size(); // Size of the string

        int i = 0; // Starting index of the window
        int j = 0; // Ending index of the window

        int ans = 0;   // Stores the maximum number of vowels
        int count = 0; // Stores the number of vowels in the current window

        // Traverse the string using pointer j.
        while(j < n) {

            // Current character entering the window.
            char ch = str[j];

            // Check whether the current character is a vowel.
            if(ch == 'a' || ch == 'e' || ch == 'i' ||
               ch == 'o' || ch == 'u') {

                // Increase vowel count because a vowel
                // has entered the current window.
                count++;
            }

            // Check whether the current window size has become k.
            if(j - i + 1 == k) {

                // Update the maximum number of vowels found so far.
                ans = max(ans, count);

                // Store the leftmost character before removing it.
                char left = str[i];

                // Move the starting pointer forward.
                // This removes the leftmost character from the window.
                i++;

                // Check whether the removed character was a vowel.
                if(left == 'a' || left == 'e' || left == 'i' ||
                   left == 'o' || left == 'u') {

                    // Decrease count because this vowel
                    // is no longer part of the current window.
                    count--;
                }
            }

            // Move the ending pointer forward.
            j++;
        }

        // Return the maximum number of vowels in any window of size k.
        return ans;
    }
};
